{"id":"bfb19ecb-854e-4535-994a-8ef2474bec65","object":"chat.completion","created":1784992464,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            children[p].append(n['id'])\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n    removed = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if n['parent'] is None:\\n            continue\\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        has_retained_child = any(cid not in removed for cid in children.get(nid, []))\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\\n        all_present = all(symbol_counts.get(req, 0) > 0 for req in required_symbols)\\n        if all_present:\\n            removed.add(nid)\\n            removal_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            symbol_counts[sym] += 1\\n    retained = sorted([n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed])\\n    return {\\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order, \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for SE-PE-01. The task is \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\". The payload contains a tree of nodes with fields: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Also required_symbols list. The goal is to remove removable nodes (but not root or required symbols) while preserving required symbols and respecting grammar validit