 # check retained children: any child not removed?\n        has_retained_child = any(cid not in removed for cid in children.get(nid, []))\n        if has_retained_child:\n            continue\n        # tentative removal: check required symbols\n        # decrement symbol count\n        sym = n['symbol']\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\n        # check if all required symbols still have count > 0\n        all_present = all(symbol_counts.get(req, 0) > 0 for req in required_symbols)\n        if all_present:\n            # actually remove\n            removed.add(nid)\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # revert count\n            symbol_counts[sym] += 1\n    retained = sorted([n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed])\n    return {\"removed_node_ids\": removal_order, \"retained_node_ids\": retained}\n\nTest with given fixtures? Should work.\n\nNow produce JSON. Remove extra whitespace maybe.\n\nI'll write the code as a string, then use json.dumps on dict. But I need to embed that string into the response. Since I am the assistant, I can just output the JSON directly. Let me do that.\n\nNote: The problem says \"Do not use Markdown code fences. Do not add a preamble, explanation, or trailing text.\" So output only the JSON object.\n\nI'll produce:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            children[p].append(n['id'])\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n    removed = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if n['parent'] is None:\\n            co